# T-654: a hold on a field in a frame is a hold on a field: the daemon's hit test follows the frame, the field takes
# the focus (the keyboard comes) and the card is told "editable", so its menu is the editing one.
id: frame-field-hold
section: Keyboard and text
item: A hold on a field inside a frame (jihad-frame-field.html): the daemon and the page's commands both call it editable (the editing menu, not the page's), the field takes the focus and the keyboard comes up; a hold on the frame's plain text stays the page's
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-frame-field.html
kit: cavekit-ui-shell.md R7
wait rect f 20
calibrate outer
hold-off f 60 30 1500
wait line 'hold at .* editable=0' 8
wait line 'hold: editable=false' 8
dismiss 640 40
wait still f 4
sample before f
hold-off f 100 90 1500
wait line 'hold at .* editable=1' 8
wait line 'hold: editable=true' 8
# what the card was told is what picks its menu ("page-hold" with editable true: Paste and Select All); the frame's
# picture changes where the menu and the caret stand, and the frame is kept for the eye
wait line 'notify: page-hold: {"editable":true' 8
wait differs f before 5
expect region-changed f before
expect keyboard up 8
shoot field-menu
# the field already focused (a tap first), then the hold: the daemon's frame lookups with the focus inside the frame
dismiss 640 40
chrome kb-hide
expect keyboard down 8
tap-off f 100 90
expect keyboard up 8
hold-off f 100 90 1500
wait line 'hold at .* editable=1 wasFocused=1' 8
wait line 'hold: editable=true' 8
